{
  "id": "COMPOUND:33450 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Turicine is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Turicine acts as a target for Caspase-2, which in turn is targeted by Swinholide A and another compound, 6-[(2S)-2,3-dihydroxy-3-methylbutyl]-7-methoxychromen-2-one. These compounds all ultimately target DNA polymerase iota, indicating a chain of molecular interactions that lead to the activation or modulation of this enzyme. The presence of multiple pathways converging on DNA polymerase iota suggests a potential role for Turicine in the regulation of this enzyme, possibly through the activation of Caspase-2, which could influence the expression or activity of DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Turicine may influence DNA polymerase iota, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
